      "writtenOn": "2018-01-09T02:02:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is almost certainly fine for multiple reasons :\n・For all non-VPN networks mAllowedUids is null.\n・There can only be one active VPN at a time.\n・This is what the current code does, but in another place.\n・VPN apps will typically add one or two of these ranges. If a VPN app adds many it can be viewed as its own responsibility for making things slow.\n\nThat being said, it\u0027s true that this may constitute a possible DoS attack against the system as this code is being run by the connectivity service. It\u0027s local and there would be a very obvious culprit in the active VPN app, and I really wonder what an app would stand to get from such an attack - maybe some ransomware ? Maybe we want to add a check in l.860 for some reasonably maximum number of ranges to counter that possibility, what do you think ?\n\nIn any case this should not be making things worse ; the attack, if relevant, already exists in the current code.",
      "parentUuid": "f70ab762_07d142ea",
