      "writtenOn": "2018-01-09T02:02:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Positively, for this change, this is the behavior we want. The reason for this is that this is exactly what the current code does, plus comments to explain how counter-intuitive it is. I did worry about the same thing and raised it with Lorenzo, and we thought this was the best course of action for the time being.\n\nThat being said I do agree that it is counter-intuitive and it should be addressed in followup changes. But this will not be very trivial, it will need encapsulation and serious unit testing. At the very least we don\u0027t want to put this into this change which is complex enough as it is, so we thought keeping the current behavior was the safer bet for the time being.",
